A commit is a permanent snapshot of your project. This lesson covers how to create commits correctly, write useful messages, and read the project history.

Staging files with git add
git add moves files from the working directory into the staging area. The staging area is a preparation zone. You choose exactly which changes go into the next commit. Files in the staging area are described as "staged" or "indexed."

# Stage a single file
git add tracker.py

# Stage multiple specific files
git add tracker.py config.py README.md

# Stage all changes in the current directory
git add .

# Check what is staged
git status
